# ==============================================================================
# Dygo Academy
# ==============================================================================

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the JWT signing secret, the anon/service_role keys derived from
# it, the Stripe secret key and the VAPID private key. Only .env.example is
# ever committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# .env.tailscale carries this machine's real tailscale IP (a personal
# network identifier) — same rationale as .env.local above, just not
# matched by the ".local" patterns since it's a separate named profile
# (see .env.local's own comments for what these profile files are).
.env.tailscale

# .env.stg is a third named profile (tailscale + Cloudflare R2), same
# rationale as .env.tailscale above -- was never actually excluded until
# now (caught 2026-09-05 while staging an unrelated commit).
.env.stg

# R2.readme was found sitting in the repo root holding a live Cloudflare
# API token, Access Key ID and Secret Access Key in plaintext -- not a
# secrets *pattern* so much as one specific leftover file, but excluded by
# name so a future `git add -A` can never pick it up. This file should be
# deleted from disk and those credentials rotated, not just gitignored.
/R2.readme

